>       It should reverse the phone-charges by dialing back the person
>       who tried to dial-in.

   Following is what we came up with to do that on Pyramid 90x with Hayes
modem... can probably be hacked for other systems.  Note that it must
be installed setuid root (so it can write to /dev/itp0) and must be
executed from login shell via exec.  To avoid problems where someone
happens to login on the line before the program calls back the original
user, it executes login when done...

